      {
        "text": "P2's broad positive shift begins in the period containing the logged pressure-setting transition at 90 seconds elapsed. Its approximately 0.4-bar magnitude agrees with the approved record, making an operating explanation plausible there. KN-OPERATING-R1 requires comparing sign, timing and affected assets, not assuming that a log explains every anomaly. The P5 comparison instead shows declining pressures, and the log coverage record supplies no verified P5 operation. The available log is incomplete, so an unrecorded operation remains unresolved. Request incident-time upstream and branch records to test whether they account for P5's sign and timing.",
