    "regional_assessments": [
      {
        "text": "P5 ST3-ST5 show paired reductions of approximately 0.43-0.62 bar in the final one-second period, compared with approximately 0.10-0.16 bar at ST1/ST8 and smaller changes at the compared P4/P6 locations. The central pattern crosses both shared data connections, supporting a physical-event review under KN-INDEPENDENCE-R1. Nevertheless, distinct connections do not rule out a shared operating cause, and the short ending cannot establish sustained behavior or a leak. Separately, health claims identify one spike each at P5-ST2-A, P5-ST7-A and P5-ST7-B; these flags do not establish hardware failure. Request review of their raw readings alongside longer synchronized records and independent pressure/flow evidence. These stations identify a review focus, not a qualified inspection bracket, consistent with KN-LOCALIZATION-R1.",
